#: ../clips.rst:61
msgid "Trimming & Slicing"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:62
msgid "OpenShot provides multiple ways to adjust the start and end trim positions of a clip (also known as trimming). The most common method is to click and drag the left or right edge of a clip. Trimming can be used to remove unwanted sections from the beginning or ending of a clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:66
msgid "To **slice** a clip into smaller sections, OpenShot offers several options, including dividing or slicing a clip at the play-head (*vertical playback line*) position. Trimming and slicing clips are powerful tools that allow users to rearrange sections of video and remove unwanted parts."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:70
msgid "Here is a list of all methods for cutting and/or trimming clips in OpenShot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:76
msgid "Trim & Slice Method"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:78
msgid "**Resizing Edge**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:78
msgid "Mouse over the edge of a clip and resize it by dragging **left** or **right**. The left edge of a clip can not be resized smaller than 0.0 (*i.e. the first frame of the file*). The right edge of a clip can not be resized larger than the duration of a file (*i.e. the last frame of a file*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:79
msgid "**Slice All**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:79
msgid "When the play-head overlaps multiple clips, right-click the play-head and choose :guilabel:`Slice All`. This will cut/slice all intersecting clips on all tracks. You can also use the keyboard shortcuts :kbd:`Ctrl+Shift+K` to keep both sides, :kbd:`Ctrl+Shift+J` to keep the left side, or :kbd:`Ctrl+Shift+L` to keep the right side of the clips."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:83
msgid "**Slice Selected**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:83
msgid "When the play-head overlaps a clip, right-click the clip and choose :guilabel:`Slice`. This provides options to keep the left side, the right side, or both sides of the clip. Alternatively, use :kbd:`Ctrl+K` to keep both sides, :kbd:`Ctrl+J` to keep the left side, or :kbd:`Ctrl+L` to keep the right side."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:86
msgid "**Slice Selected (Ripple)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:86
msgid "Slice the selected clip(s) at the play-head position, keeping either the left side (shortcut: :kbd:`W`) or the right side (shortcut: :kbd:`Q`), while rippling the gap removal across the current track."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:88
msgid "**Razor Tool**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:88
msgid "The :guilabel:`razor tool` from the **Timeline Toolbar** cuts a clip at the position where it is clicked. Use :kbd:`SHIFT` to slice and keep the left side, or :kbd:`CTRL` to keep the right side."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:90
msgid "**Split File Dialog**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:90
msgid "Right-click on a file and choose :guilabel:`Split File`. This opens a dialog that allows you to create multiple clips from a single video file."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:94
msgid "Keep in mind that the above cutting methods also have :ref:`keyboard_shortcut_ref`, to save even more time."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:96
msgid "If multiple selected clips and/or transitions share the same left edge or right edge, you can drag that shared edge once to trim them together."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:100
msgid "Selections"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:101
msgid "Selecting clips and transitions on the timeline is an essential part of editing in OpenShot. Multiple selection methods are available to streamline your workflow, enabling efficient editing of clips and transitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:104
msgid "Here is a list of all methods for selecting clips in OpenShot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:110
msgid "Selection Method"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:112
msgid "**Box Selection**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:112
msgid "Click and drag a selection box around clips or transitions to select multiple items at once. Hold down :kbd:`Ctrl` to add to your current selection."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:113
msgid "**Click Selection**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:113
msgid "Click on a clip or transition to select it. This will deselect all other items unless you hold down :kbd:`Ctrl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:114
msgid "**Add to Selection**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:114
msgid "Hold down :kbd:`Ctrl` while clicking to add or remove clips from the current selection, allowing you to select non-adjacent clips."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:115
msgid "**Range Selection**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:115
msgid "Hold down :kbd:`Shift` while clicking to select a range of clips/transitions from the previous selection to the new selection. This supports ranges that span multiple tracks as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:116
msgid "**Ripple Selection**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:116
msgid "Hold down :kbd:`Alt` while clicking to ripple select all clips/transitions from your selection to the end of the track. This always adds to your current selection, even if :kbd:`Ctrl` is not pressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:117
msgid "**Clear Selection**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:117
msgid "Click anywhere on the timeline or on a new clip/transition to reset the current selection, unless :kbd:`Ctrl` is pressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:118
msgid "**Select All**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:118
msgid "Press :kbd:`Ctrl+A` to select all clips and transitions on the timeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:119
msgid "**Select None**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:119
msgid "Press :kbd:`Ctrl+Shift+A` to deselect all clips and transitions on the timeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:122
msgid "Mastering these selection techniques will streamline your editing process, especially when dealing with complex projects. For more advanced tips on selection and editing, refer to the :ref:`clips_cutting_slicing_ref` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:128
msgid "Context Menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:129
msgid "OpenShot has tons of great preset animations and clip properties, such as fading, sliding, zooming, reversing time, adjusting volume, etc... These presets can be accessed by right-clicking on a clip, revealing the context menu. A preset sets one (or more) clip properties for the user without needing to manually set the key-frame clip properties. See :ref:`clip_properties_ref`."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:134
msgid "Some presets allow the user to target either the start, end, or entire clip, and most presets allow the user to reset a specific clip property. For example, when using the :guilabel:`Audio → Volume` presets, the user has the following menu options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:138
msgid "**Reset Volume** — resets the volume to the original level."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:139
msgid "**Start of Clip** — the volume change applies at the beginning of the clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:140
msgid "**End of Clip** — the volume change applies at the end of the clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:141
msgid "**Entire Clip** — the volume change applies to the entire clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:149
msgid "Preset Name"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:151
#: ../clips.rst:539
msgid "Copy / Cut / Paste"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:151
msgid "Copy selected clip data, cut selected clips, or paste copied clip data. Copy supports full clips, effects, and keyframe groups."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:152
msgid "Align"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:152
msgid "Align the left or right edge of multiple selected clips and transitions (only shown when multiple clips are selected)."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:153
#: ../clips.rst:165
msgid "Fade"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:153
msgid "Fade the clip in or out — automatically fades video (alpha) and/or audio (volume) based on what the clip contains."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:154
#: ../clips.rst:182
msgid "Motion"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:154
msgid "Add animated motion to a clip: slide in/out, bounce, blur, wipe/focus-wipe, zoom, emphasis effects at the playhead, camera movements, and scrolling credits. Only shown for visual clips."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:155
#: ../clips.rst:417
msgid "Transform"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:155
msgid "Apply geometric presets to a clip: rotate/flip, crop, or snap to a corner layout. Also provides a **No Transform** reset. Only shown for visual clips."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:156
#: ../clips.rst:318
msgid "Look"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:156
msgid "Apply visual style presets: color grades, film grain, analog tape, sharpen, blur, shadow, and glow effects. Includes **Adjust Colors** (Color Wheels editor) and **Analyze Colors** (video scopes). Only shown for visual clips."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:157
#: ../clips.rst:249
msgid "Speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:157
msgid "Reverse, repeat, speed up, or slow down video. Includes Freeze and Freeze & Zoom options."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:158
#: ../clips.rst:365
msgid "Audio"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:158
msgid "Control audio properties: adjust volume levels, fade volume in/out, separate audio channels, show/hide the timeline waveform, or open the Audio Levels scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:159
#: ../clips.rst:392
msgid "Slice"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:159
msgid "Cut the clip at the play-head position, with options to keep either side, both sides, or ripple-delete one side. Only shown when the playhead overlaps the clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:160
#: ../clips.rst:531
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:160
msgid "Show the properties panel for a clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:161
#: ../clips.rst:563
msgid "Remove Clip"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:161
msgid "Remove a clip from the timeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:166
msgid "The :guilabel:`Fade` preset creates a smooth fade-in or fade-out on the selected clip. It automatically fades **video** (alpha/opacity) and/or **audio** (volume) depending on what the clip contains — a video clip gets both, an audio-only clip gets only a volume fade, and an image clip gets only an alpha fade."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:170
msgid ":guilabel:`No Fade` — removes all fade keyframes."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:171
msgid ":guilabel:`Fade In` → :guilabel:`Fast` / :guilabel:`Slow` — fades from transparent/silent at the start of the clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:172
msgid ":guilabel:`Fade Out` → :guilabel:`Fast` / :guilabel:`Slow` — fades to transparent/silent at the end of the clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:173
msgid ":guilabel:`Fade In and Out` → :guilabel:`Fast` / :guilabel:`Slow` — applies both a fade-in at the start and a fade-out at the end."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:175
msgid "Fast fades span approximately 1 second; Slow fades span approximately 3 seconds. See :ref:`clip_alpha_ref` and :ref:`clip_volume_ref` key-frames."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:178
msgid "**Usage Example:** Applying a fade-out to a video clip to gently conclude a scene."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:179
msgid "**Tip:** Fade and Volume fade are independent — use :guilabel:`Fade` for a combined video+audio fade, or use :guilabel:`Audio → Volume` to fade only the audio."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:183
msgid "The :guilabel:`Motion` menu adds animated movement to visual clips using keyframe presets. It is organized into several submenus. See :ref:`clip_location_x_ref` and :ref:`clip_scale_x_ref` key-frames."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:186
msgid ":guilabel:`No Motion` — removes all motion keyframes from the clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:187
msgid ":guilabel:`In` — entrance animations applied at the start of the clip:"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:189
msgid "**Back In** (From Bottom / Left / Right / Top) — clip overshoots and springs back into position."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:190
msgid "**Blur In** — clip fades in from a motion blur."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:191
msgid "**Bounce In** (Center / From Bottom / Left / Right / Top) — clip bounces as it enters."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:192
msgid "**Focus Wipe In** (Circle Expand / Circle Shrink / From Bottom / Left / Right / Top) — clip is revealed by a wipe while sharpening from blur into focus."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:193
msgid "**Pop In** — clip scales up quickly from nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:194
msgid "**Slide In** (From Bottom / Left / Right / Top) — clip slides onto the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:195
msgid "**Spiral In** — clip rotates in while scaling up."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:196
msgid "**Wipe In** (Circle Expand / Circle Shrink / From Bottom / Left / Right / Top) — clip is revealed by a wipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:198
msgid ":guilabel:`Out` — exit animations applied at the end of the clip (mirrors the In options: Back Out, Blur Out, Bounce Out, Focus Wipe Out, Pop Out, Slide Out, Spiral Out, Wipe Out)."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:200
msgid ":guilabel:`Emphasis` — short attention-grabbing animations **inserted at the current playhead position** (not applied across the whole clip). Useful for mid-clip highlights: **Bounce**, **Flash**, **Heartbeat**, **Jello**, **Pulse**, **Rubber Band**, **Shake X**, **Shake Y**, **Swing**, **Tada**, **Wobble**."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:202
msgid ":guilabel:`Camera` — simulates camera movement on the clip by animating scale and position:"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:204
msgid "**Zoom** → In / Out — a simple push-in or pull-out."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:205
msgid "**Pan** → Auto Direction / Left to Right / Right to Left / Top to Bottom / Bottom to Top — a lateral camera pan. *Auto Direction* picks the best direction based on the clip's aspect ratio."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:206
msgid "**Zoom & Pan** → In or Out, with directional variants — combines a zoom with a pan (Ken Burns style). *Auto Direction* picks the best direction based on the clip's aspect ratio."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:208
msgid ":guilabel:`Credits` — scrolling credit animations: **Scroll Up** and **Scroll Down**."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:210
msgid "**Tip:** Emphasis presets are placed at the current playhead position, so position the playhead over the moment you want to highlight before applying one."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:211
msgid "**Tip:** Camera presets use *Auto Direction* by default, which picks the optimal pan direction for wide or tall media to avoid black bars."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:216
msgid "Rotate"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:217
msgid "The :guilabel:`Transform → Rotate` submenu introduces easy rotation and flipping of clips. It enables orientation adjustment by rotating and flipping a clip for creative visual transformations. See :ref:`clip_rotation_ref` key-frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:221
msgid ":guilabel:`No Rotation` — removes any rotation keyframes."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:222
msgid ":guilabel:`Rotate 90 (Right)` — rotates the clip 90 degrees clockwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:223
msgid ":guilabel:`Rotate 90 (Left)` — rotates the clip 90 degrees counterclockwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:224
msgid ":guilabel:`Rotate 180 (Flip)` — flips the clip upside down."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:226
msgid "**Usage Example:** Rotating a photo or video by 90 degrees (a portrait video to a landscape)."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:227
msgid "**Usage Example:** If your video is upside down, rotate it by 180 degrees to correct the orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:232
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:233
msgid "The :guilabel:`Transform → Layout` submenu adjusts the size of a clip and snaps it to a chosen corner of the screen, useful for picture-in-picture or watermark effects. See :ref:`clip_location_x_ref`, :ref:`clip_scale_x_ref`, :guilabel:`Margin`, and :guilabel:`Corner Radius` key-frames."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:238
msgid ":guilabel:`Reset Layout` — removes any layout keyframes."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:239
msgid ":guilabel:`1/4 Size` — positions the clip at 1/4 of the screen in the Center, Top Left, Top Right, Bottom Left, or Bottom Right corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:240
msgid ":guilabel:`Show All (Maintain Ratio)` — fits the entire clip frame within the screen while preserving its aspect ratio."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:241
msgid ":guilabel:`Show All (Distort)` — stretches the entire clip frame to fill the screen, ignoring aspect ratio."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:243
msgid "**Usage Example:** Placing a logo in the corner of a video using the layout preset."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:244
msgid "**Tip:** Use :guilabel:`Margin` to create an inset layout area for a clip, and :guilabel:`Corner Radius` to round picture-in-picture camera clips without adding a Mask effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:246
msgid "**Tip:** Combine with animation presets for dynamic transitions involving resizing and repositioning."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:250
msgid "The :guilabel:`Speed` menu manipulates clip playback speed, allowing for reverse playback, time-lapse, slow-motion, freezes, and looping effects. See :ref:`clip_time_ref` key-frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:253
msgid ":guilabel:`Reset Speed` — restores the clip to normal 1× speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:254
msgid ":guilabel:`Reverse` — plays the clip backwards at normal speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:255
msgid ":guilabel:`Speed Up` → Forward / Backward → 2×, 4×, 8×, 16× — speeds up playback in either direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:256
msgid ":guilabel:`Slow Down` → Forward / Backward → 1/2×, 1/4×, 1/8×, 1/16× — slows down playback in either direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:257
msgid ":guilabel:`Repeat` — see below."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:258
msgid ":guilabel:`Freeze` — freezes on the frame at the current playhead position for 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 20, or 30 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:259
msgid ":guilabel:`Freeze && Zoom` — freezes and simultaneously zooms in on that frozen frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:261
msgid "**Slow motion** — :guilabel:`Slow Down → 1/2×` or :guilabel:`1/4×` for dreamy or dramatic footage."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:262
msgid "**Time-lapse** — :guilabel:`Speed Up → 8×` or :guilabel:`16×` to compress hours into seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:263
msgid "**Speed ramp** — use the :guilabel:`Timing` tool to drag clip edges and create a natural-feeling speed change; OpenShot scales all keyframes automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:264
msgid "**Tip:** Combine :guilabel:`Freeze` with :guilabel:`Speed Up` for an impact-freeze-then-fast-forward effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:269
msgid "Repeat"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:270
msgid "Use :guilabel:`Speed → Repeat` to play a clip multiple times, without building the time curve by hand. OpenShot writes the needed :guilabel:`Time` keyframes for you (you can edit them later)."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:273
msgid "**Menu path**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:275
msgid ":guilabel:`Speed → Repeat → Loop → Forward` – plays left to right, then starts again from the beginning"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:276
msgid ":guilabel:`Speed → Repeat → Loop → Reverse` – plays right to left, then starts again from the end"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:277
msgid ":guilabel:`Speed → Repeat → Ping-Pong → Forward` – forward, then backward, then forward…"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:278
msgid ":guilabel:`Speed → Repeat → Ping-Pong → Reverse` – backward, then forward, then backward…"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:279
msgid ":guilabel:`Custom…` – opens a dialog for extra options (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:281
msgid "Counts are **finite** (2x, 3x, 4x, 5x, 8x, 10x, or a custom number). Example: “Forward then Back and stop” = :guilabel:`Ping-Pong → Forward → 2x`."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:284
msgid "**What gets repeated**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:286
msgid "Repeat always acts on the **currently trimmed** in/out of the clip."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:287
msgid "The :guilabel:`Time` curve is stamped as a simple shape: - Loop Forward = rising saw - Loop Reverse = falling saw - Ping-Pong = triangle (direction flips each pass)"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:291
msgid "To avoid a double frame at the seam, the last frame of each pass is not duplicated."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:293
msgid "**Keyframes during Repeat**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:295
msgid "When you use Repeat, OpenShot will also **repeat other keyframes** found inside the trimmed section (location, scale, effects, etc.) into each pass so your animations stay in sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:296
msgid "Repeated keyframes keep their relative timing inside each pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:298
msgid "**Custom Repeat** (dialog options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:300
msgid ":guilabel:`Pattern:` Loop | Ping-Pong"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:301
msgid ":guilabel:`Direction:` Forward | Reverse"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:302
msgid ":guilabel:`Passes:` integer (2 or more). This is the number of times it will play."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:303
msgid ":guilabel:`Delay:` number + units [frames | ms | sec]. This is an optional delay between each repeated pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:304
msgid ":guilabel:`Speed Ramp (%):` % speed change per pass (optional). Positive speeds up each pass; negative slows down each pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:306
msgid "**Reset**"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:308
msgid ":guilabel:`Speed → Reset Speed` completely removes any Time curve (including Repeat) and restores the clip to its original playback, **without deleting your original non-Time keyframes**."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:312
msgid "Timing Tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:313
msgid "Another way to change a clip's speed is with the :guilabel:`Timing` tool on the timeline toolbar. Enable the clock icon and drag a clip's edges. Lengthening the clip slows playback, while shotening it speeds the clip up. All keyframes on the clip and its effects are scaled so their relative positions remain intact."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:319
msgid "The :guilabel:`Look` menu applies one-click visual style presets to clips. All presets work by adding or updating effects on the clip — you can inspect or animate them further in the Properties dock. The menu is organized into four submenus plus two direct actions at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:323
msgid ":guilabel:`Reset Look` — removes all Look-managed effects (Color Grade, Film Grain, Analog Tape, Sharpen, Blur, Shadow, Glow) from the selected clips in a single step."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:326
msgid "**Color** — applies a :guilabel:`Color Grade` effect with one of four quick presets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:328
msgid "**Auto Contrast** — boosts contrast by lifting shadows and pulling highlights."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:329
msgid "**Lift Shadows** — brightens the dark areas of the image."
msgstr ""

#: ../clips.rst:330
msgid "**Warm Up** — shifts the color balance toward warm orange/amber tones."
